rsx draw engine + metal: a Z24S8 zeta read as A8R8G8B8 is converted on the GPU, not stored through guest memory.

Resistance 3 rebuilds depth from the bytes of its depth buffers several times a frame: the 1920x704 Z24S8 zeta at
0x00E00000 and the 960x704 one at 0x01380000 (two crossbars), each read as a linear unnormalized A8R8G8B8 texture of
the zeta's own pitch; the 960x704 one twice a frame while it is still the bound zeta (depth writes off). The engine served each read by storing the depth target into guest memory
(eng_zdepth_to_guest: submit_and_wait, a GPU readback, a CPU conversion), then hashing and decoding the texture again:
2.1 GB of decode per 120 frames for those two addresses, more than half of the FIFO/present thread.

The backend now has an optional depth_as_argb(depth, w, h): a recorded pass, in command order like depth_snapshot,
that writes an R8G8B8A8 texture with what the store plus the decode would give (R = depth bits 15..8, G = 7..0,
B = 0 for the stencil byte, A = 23..16; round(d * 0xFFFFFF) taken exactly with 64-bit integers, as the double
store takes it). The unit samples a surface_view of it with its crossbar. The engine uses it for a texture at the
zeta's address that is A8R8G8B8 linear, 2D, one level, of the zeta's pitch, inside the written clip, the bound zeta
included (the conversion takes the depth the draws so far left, as the store reads it back); it keeps one conversion per zeta and makes a new one after the next depth write or clear.
Anything else, a backend without the hook, or PS3RECOMP_ENG_DEPTH_VIA_GUEST=1, stores through guest memory as before.
Guest memory is not refreshed for these reads (guest_dirty stays set for any other reader).
TODO: the stencil byte is 0, as the store writes it; Z16 read as a colour format still goes through guest memory.

test_rsx_draw_engine: the read goes to the hook with no readback, store or upload; the same texture until the next
depth write, then a new one with the old released; the zeta still bound is converted too and reused while no draw writes
depth (3 checks fail with the bound zeta excluded); another pitch and a refusing backend take the store as before.
test_metal_depth_as_argb (new): edge depths (0, 1, subnormal, rounding ties) convert byte for byte as the store plus
rsx_texture_decode, and the 0xAA93 view samples as the uploaded texture does.
Measured (scripted run, Home level, stick turn, 2 runs each): 26.1-26.5 -> 29.4-29.5 fps, standing 30.0 (the game's
cap); present thread busy 652 -> ~430 samples of 6 s. The bound zeta was left to the store at first: that kept
692 MB of A8R8G8B8 decode per 120 frames (two reads a frame); with it converted too, ~1 MB, eng_texture_slot
~700 -> ~280 ms per 120 frames, turn 29.4 -> 29.9 fps, sink_bind_textures 264-331 -> 130-143 samples of 6 s. Frames match the store path (Susan's lantern, shadows, light).

Upstream: PR #499 (same change, generic wording; drop this patch when the pin has it).

